<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/4th-century-bce">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Maling</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">342 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/4th-century-bce">4th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Maling was fought in 342 BCE between the State of Qi and the State of Wei, which had attacked Han. The Qi strategist <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sun-bin">Sun Bin</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/feigned-retreat">feigned retreat</a>, reducing the number of campfires each day to suggest desertion, and ambushed the pursuing Wei army in a narrow pass at Maling. The Wei general <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pang-juan">Pang Juan</a> died and the crown prince was captured, ending Wei's dominance among the states.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-maling.jpg" alt="Battle of Maling" width="320" height="208" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: SY · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Battle_of_Maling.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
